## ⚠ Two things to read before anything else

### 1. This app cannot run yet

**Magik is not implemented.** `<%= magik_version %>` is a RubyGems name-reservation release: there
is no `App.define`, no `model`, no `screen`, no router, no server and no database code. `magik
server`, `magik test` and `magik check` exit `1` with `MAGIK_CLI_COMMAND_NOT_IMPLEMENTED`.

You can write declarations, docs and a plan today. You cannot boot, migrate, render or test. Check
rather than trust that — if it has stopped being true, this section is the first thing to delete:

```bash
magik version --json     # {"version":"<%= magik_version %>","status":"spec only",…}
magik help               # every command, each marked `ready` or `planned`
```

The one thing that does work today is the shipped documentation:

```bash
magik docs path          # the local docs directory — point grep/glob/read at it
magik docs list          # every page and its slug
```

