### 2. This app has not been set up yet

Building a Magik app is three steps, and you have done one:

```
magik new <%= app_name %>     ✓ done — static boilerplate, written by the CLI
/setup-project      ← YOU ARE HERE. An interview, run once, that makes this app yours
/feature            then this, forever — one slice at a time, gate green each run
```

`magik new` wrote a **generic** scaffold. It knows nothing about what you are building — no domains,
no entities, no plan. Open a Claude Code session here and run:

```
/setup-project
```

It interviews you about the product and then writes [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md),
[`docs/PLAN.md`](docs/PLAN.md), the project half of [`docs/FEATURE.md`](docs/FEATURE.md) and the
project half of `CLAUDE.md`. **It asks before it writes** — a domain model guessed from an app's
name is the most expensive mistake available here.

`/setup-project` removes this section on its first successful run. While it is here, the app is
still generic.

